      "writtenOn": "2020-02-07T14:07:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "final too, probably\n\nI assume this isn\u0027t dependent on anything that may not be started at the point when the class is initialized?\n\nAlso, that this isn\u0027t going to introduce a delay where you wouldn\u0027t want it (otherwise, you might want to revert to lazily creating it in onCreate() with a \"synchronized (PacService.class) {}\" block ...?).\n\nI also have to assume PacNative is thread safe (because shared) OR there are higher-level guarantees that mean PacService is instantiated once and only one thread is ever in resolvePacFile, startPacSupport, stopPacSupport, setCurrentProxyScript.\n\nAlternative suggestion: if PacNative is inherently a singleton, then I think it should be the one handling the single instance. e.g. PacNative.getInstance() rather than having it determined by the PacService having a static reference.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "31a86524ed1699db7f23c1c10b38a7a8a2b097b9",
