      },
      "lineNbr": 34,
      "author": {
        "id": 1021004
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-07T14:54:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "creating PacNative just loads the JNI library and doesn\u0027t depend on anything else. There\u0027s not really any difference between creating it as a static vs lazily in onCreate here - the service class is going to be touched for the first time right before onCreate is called anyhow.\n\nPacNative is thread safe, it deals with locking internally.\n\nYes, it would probably be nicer to have PacNative.getInstance() here.",
      "parentUuid": "0cdf6254_fdeecd05",
